      "id": "claim_9e9407e56f4b454a82d4203234973766",
      "statement": "REVIEW.md makes packages/workshop-backend and the workshop-shared public API the highest-scrutiny kernel: every exported member needs a doc comment (types, consts, functions — not just interfaces), hand-written interfaces mirroring RPC interfaces plus as-unknown-as casts are rejected in favor of deriving from the real type, existing mechanisms are preferred over parallel ones, and large kernel changes are split so backend/shared can be reviewed apart from UI.",
